[Music]  New York University is one of the most  liberal schools in America maybe the  world but even there at least one person  is continuing to refuse to conform and  it's made life hard for him ironically  he is a professor of global Liberal  Studies his name is Michel recktenwald  he's suing the school and several other  professors he accuses them of launching  a harassment campaign against him after  he condemned political correctness on  campus that professor Michel recktenwald  joins us now professor thanks for coming  on thanks for having me Tucker so tell  us what you did to earn the ire of your  colleagues well what I did is started an  anonymous Twitter account and I started  tweeting criticisms of PC culture social  justice ideology on campus which was  really coming home to roost at NYU with  the enforcement of a bias reporting  hotline safe spaces the no platforming  or shutting down of speakers like Ian  Ian Oppel Asst and so forth and so I  started tweeting and all hell broke  loose so what kinds of things did you  tweet did you threaten anyone with  violence or tried to prevent other  people from talking not at all I merely  made criticisms about what was happening  not just at NYU but all across the  country and as you know the the semester  and the year went on I was indicated by  what took place over the year 2016-17  with as the campus craziness escalated  and you know you had riots by the time  Berkeley happened and so on and so yeah  so yeah I mean I was just making  critiques of an institutional  ideological adoption and the mechanisms  to enforce it I mentioned no persons by  name no groups no races no idea  identities at all and I was immediately  within two days of an interview  appearing I was called into the dean's  office and I was told that the interview  had nothing to do with my Twitter  account or the publicity I was receiving  and yet immediately it went to that  topic and I was told that people were  concerned about my mental well-being so  because you disagreed with that because  like this thing I must be crazy yeah  because I disagreed with them and I was  put on paid leave it really strongly  encouraged to take a paid leave of  absence to upset myself from campus  immediately and then a committee calling  themselves the diversity equity and  inclusion group denounced me hoarse yes  they denounced me in a doublespeak  Orwellian condemnation in which they  said I was guilty of for the structure  of my thinking so basically I had the  wrong kinds of thoughts so the inclusion  committee excluded you they excluded me  that's why I call them the conformity  inequity and exclusion group there are  so many questions here but I can't  resist asking did any of your colleagues  secretly approach you and say you know  you're telling some truth here no either  they are true believers or they're cowed  and acquiescence by the others it's a  very very chilling effect that's going  on on campuses today  you can't voice disagreement with some  of these policies without being called a  racist sexist or Satan himself as I was  called so how how can you think clearly  if conformity is required  you can't think that's the problem it's  it's about curtailing different  perspectives and different avenues of  thought and this is antithetical to the  mission of the University and that's  exactly what I was complaining about  well if these people ever had power I  think I think a lot of people would die  actually those are those are  authoritarian impulses so what's your  response to them now my response now is  that I after I got back from the leave I  was assailed in a series of blistering  emails I was attacked roundly for  nothing I mean I never spoke to any of  these people by name or directly at all  and they started to attack me calling me  racist sexist misogynist Satan you know  short pants white boy fragile white male  while saying that I was a sexist I was  basically pelted with sexist and racist  epithets you know it  one thing to stand up and take a  position that a lot of people disagree  with but to take a position against  everyone you work around takes a special  kind of courage and I just admire that  and I I wanted to say that you and good  luck thank you professor thank you

